From: hawkff <109485367+hawkff@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 08:52:01 +0000
Subject: Do not resolve link hosts through the system resolver

When another app opened a link, or a web app was launched, the browser
resolved the host name of the link in the background with
InetAddress.getByName() to warm up the DNS cache before any tab existed.
That lookup runs through the Android system resolver, outside the browser
network stack, so it ignores the secure DNS setting and any proxy
configured in the browser, and it reveals the host to the system resolver
before the user's settings apply. WarmupManager no longer performs the
lookup, for every link, including links that open in regular tabs. The
browser resolves the host itself when it loads the page, so the first
connection for a link from another app starts slightly later.

